# Reports are generated. Almost all of them are scratch and stay out of the
# repo.
*
!.gitignore

# EXCEPT the dev-set evaluation result, which IS committed. The README quotes
# these numbers, and a quoted number with no artifact behind it is a claim
# nobody can check. tests/test_m5_eval.py compares a live run against this
# file, so a regression shows up as a diff rather than as a README that
# quietly stopped being true.
#
# It is 3KB and deterministic: same seed, same config, same bytes.
#
# reports/eval-holdout/ IS committed, and this comment previously said it would
# not be. Changed deliberately: every other quoted number in this project has an
# artifact behind it (results.json, bench.md, ai_loop.json), and a holdout figure
# is the one number that most needs to be checkable rather than trusted. It is
# written once and never regenerated.
!eval/
eval/*
!eval/results.json
!eval/results.md
# throughput.md is committed on the bench.md principle, not the results.json
# one: durations differ run to run, so this is evidence of a real run on a
# stated machine rather than a byte-stable artifact. It exists because the
# holdout was run BEFORE the runner was instrumented and so has no throughput
# figure at all - committing the dev one is what makes that absence checkable
# instead of a claim. tests/test_timing.py 22 asserts the holdout still has no
# counterpart to this file.
!eval/throughput.md
!eval-holdout/
eval-holdout/*
!eval-holdout/results.json
!eval-holdout/results.md

# bench.md is committed for the same reason: the README quotes its throughput
# figures, and the machine spec in its header is what makes them a measurement
# rather than a boast. Durations differ run to run - that is what a median of
# three is for - so this file is evidence of a real run on a stated machine,
# not a byte-stable artifact like results.json.
!bench.md

# The M7 loop result is committed for the same reason: the README quotes the
# 27/507 ceiling and the adversarial zero, and a quoted number with no artifact
# behind it is unfalsifiable. Deterministic - no model is involved.
!ai/
ai/*
!ai/ai_loop.json

# The rendered queue is committed - the README links it and the screenshots come
# from it. state.db is NOT: it is a build output of `make demo-state`, it is
# large, and a committed database would drift from the code that writes it.
!ui/
ui/*
!ui/queue.html
!ui/evidence-queue.png
!ui/streamlit-queue.png
!ui/evidence-panel.png
